    "label": "thm:upper_bound",
    "number": "Theorem 1.1",
    "quote": "Consider the full decision set $\\Acal$. For $1\\leq S\\leq K$ and any strongly observable directed graph $G=([K],E)$, there exists an algorithm $\\pi$ that achieves regret \\E[\\reg(\\pi)] = \\widetilde{O}(S\\sqrt{T} + \\sqrt{\\alpha ST})."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Paper's S is combinatorial size m; K is number of base arms; alpha is independence number. Regret is E[max_v sum <v - v^t, r^t>], i.e. expected regret against best fixed decision."
